# Test case for BDSensor pin alias resolution
#
# Verifies that BDSensor's sda_pin / scl_pin / endstop_pin lookups
# correctly unwrap [board_pins] aliases before sending the resolved
# hardware pin names to the MCU. The driver communicates with the MCU
# over the bd_sensor protocol, so the dictionary used here must come
# from a firmware build with src-y += BD_sensor.c enabled.
CONFIG bdsensor_alias.cfg
DICTIONARY stm32h723xx-bdsensor.dict

# Start by homing the printer.
G28
G1 F6000

# Z / X / Y moves
G1 Z1
G1 X1
G1 Y1

# Run a probe to exercise the BDSensor endstop wrapper. If the alias
# lookup is broken, the bd_sensor_register MCU command would have failed
# at startup with "Unable to find pin PROBE_SENSOR".
PROBE
QUERY_PROBE

# Bed mesh exercises the probe through ProbePointsHelper (which now
# reads use_probe_xy_offsets from the section config) and tests the
# scl_pin lookup as well.
BED_MESH_CALIBRATE
G1 Z5 X0 Y0
